## Decisions log — standing instruction

Whenever you make or observe a hard-to-reverse decision in this repo (a
real trade-off between alternatives, a scope cut with a non-obvious reason,
a "why not the more standard approach" call) — **append an entry to
`docs/decisions.md` before ending the turn, without being asked.** This is
load-bearing: it's the only reason project decisions survive past the
session that made them. See STANDARDS.md for why.
{% if needs_api %}

## Working in a git worktree

**Run `node scripts/setup-worktree-env.js` automatically, without being
asked, whenever you set up a new worktree for this repo.** It assigns
non-colliding host ports per worktree so multiple checkouts can run
`docker compose up` concurrently. Idempotent, safe to re-run.
